<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept cocoa exports up 21.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Indonesia 1996 Jan-Sept cocoa exports up 21.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's exports of cocoa beans rose 21.1 percent to $192.3 million in the first nine months of 1996 from $158.8 million in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p>The finance ministry released the data ahead of President Suharto's unveiling of the 1997/98 (April-March) state budget in parliament on Monday.</p>
<p>Indonesia is the world's third largest cocoa producer after the Ivory Coast and Ghana.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom + 6221 384-6364</p>
